WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:02.470
- [Instructor] We're told each big square

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:05.420
below represents one whole.

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.560
Express the shaded area

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.180
as both a mixed number and a decimal.

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:13.160
So pause this video and
see if you can do that.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.190
What would this be as a mixed number,

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:17.140
and then what would it be as a decimal?

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.520
All right, now let's do it together.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.500
So let's first start
with the mixed number.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.980
So we see that we have one whole here,

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.090
the whole thing is filled out,

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:28.820
so this is going to be one whole,

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:30.700
and then over here, we have part

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:33.040
of this second whole filled out,

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.600
and it looks like we're dividing

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.190
this whole into 10 equal sections,

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:41.370
and then two of those are filled out.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:44.150
So as a mixed number, we have one

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:49.150
and then you have two
of the 10ths filled out.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:53.770
So this is gonna be 1
2/10, and we're done.

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:55.520
You can see here, this
is split into 10ths,

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.460
and we filled in two of them.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:59.770
Now, what about as a decimal?

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:02.860
Well, we could just express
1 2/10 as a decimal.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:04.850
We could say, hey, that's going to be one,

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.770
and then we get to the 10th place,

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:08.470
and then how many 10ths do we have?

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:09.960
We have two of them.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.260
So that's going to be 1.2.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:13.823
Let's do another example.

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:16.830
So here, this is a
little bit more involved.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.830
They say, once again, each big square

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:21.050
below represents one whole.

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:22.290
And once again, they want us

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:25.870
to express the shaded area as
both a fraction and a decimal.

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:28.193
So pause this video and have a go at this.

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:31.930
All right, so let's start
with the fraction again.

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:35.350
So we have one whole, two wholes,

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:38.170
and then partially shaded
in this third whole,

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:39.760
so if I'm gonna express
this as a fraction,

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.330
really it's going to be a mixed number,

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:45.500
I would say that this over
here, this is two wholes.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.140
Now, this third whole is
only partially filled in,

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:51.530
and we can see that it has
been divided into 100ths,

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:53.540
you can see it's a 10 by 10 grid,

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:57.190
so each of these squares
represent 100th of a whole,

00:01:57.190 --> 00:02:00.560
and how many of these
100ths are filled in?

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:05.560
Well, let's see, you have
10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70,

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:16.130
and then you have 71, two, three, four.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:21.130
We can see that 74 of
the 100ths are filled in.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:23.230
So as a mixed number, this

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:28.103
whole thing would represent 2 74/100.

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:31.280
Now, if we wanna write it as a decimal,

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:32.760
we would have two wholes,

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:34.780
and then we could go to the 10ths place.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:37.560
You could just write two
and 74 100ths like that,

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:38.920
if you're pretty familiar with it.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:39.950
You could also think about it

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.960
in terms of how many 10ths and
how many 100ths did you have.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:47.440
We have one, two, three,

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:52.000
four, five, six, seven 10ths,

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.420
and then we have four
more 100ths beyond that,

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:58.770
so you could think of it as
74 100ths or 7/10 and 400ths,

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:00.563
but either way, we are done.

